                    r2_s3_text: `Establish a Community Advisory Board (delay decision)`,
                    r2_s3_hint: `Buys time but does not resolve the fork threat. Community patience wears thin.`,
                    r2_s4_text: `Decline to open-source VeloxCore`,
                    r2_s4_hint: `Preserves IP fully but fork campaign accelerates. Competitive alternative likely within 12 months.`,
                    r3_title: `Round 3 — Portfolio Optimization (Months 13-18)`,
                    r3_desc: `Three low-value patents approach renewal deadlines. A <b>European competitor</b> has filed patents overlapping your anomaly-detection technology (P-003). <b>Hanbit Robotics</b> (South Korea) requests a non-exclusive license for logistics automation. VeloxEdge v5.0 needs a freedom-to-operate clearance.<br><br>Optimize your portfolio: what to maintain, what to lapse, what to challenge.`,
                    r3_s1_text: `Maintain all patents and file FTO clearance study`,
                    r3_s1_hint: `Safe but expensive. 34K in maintenance plus 40K FTO study. Full coverage.`,
                    r3_s2_text: `Lapse low-value patents (P-004, P-006) and redirect budget`,
                    r3_s2_hint: `Saves 34K/year. Freed budget can fund competitor challenge or new filings.`,
                    r3_s3_text: `Challenge European competitor patent at EPO`,
                    r3_s3_hint: `Cost 50K, 12-24 months, ~45% success. Protects core anomaly-detection space.`,
                    r3_s4_text: `Design around competitor patent for v5.0`,
                    r3_s4_hint: `Cost 20K per patent, preserves FTO without confrontation. Lower risk approach.`,
                    r4_title: `Round 4 — Ecosystem and Standards (Months 19-24)`,
                    r4_desc: `The <b>Industrial AI Interoperability Consortium</b> is developing a new edge-AI standard. Two of your patents (P-001, P-003) appear essential. Declaring SEP status requires <b>FRAND licensing commitments</b> — constraining your pricing but potentially establishing the standard on your preferred architecture.<br><br>Budget is tight: you can afford only 2 of 3 new v5.0 patent filings.`,
                    r4_s1_text: `Join consortium and declare SEP with FRAND commitment`,
                    r4_s1_hint: `Major influence on standard. Strong moat. But FRAND constrains future licensing flexibility.`,
                    r4_s2_text: `Join consortium without declaring SEP`,
                    r4_s2_hint: `Participate and influence direction. Keep full licensing flexibility. Less industry credibility.`,
                    r4_s3_text: `Decline consortium participation`,
                    r4_s3_hint: `Preserve full autonomy. Risk that standard develops without your technology. Isolation risk.`,
                    r4_s4_text: `Join and offer a Defensive Patent Pledge`,
                    r4_s4_hint: `Ecosystem goodwill, protects open-source community. Maintains assertion against direct competitors.`,
                    r5_title: `Round 5 — M and A Readiness and Exit Optimization (Months 25-36)`,
                    r5_desc: `A <b>major industrial automation conglomerate</b> is conducting due diligence for acquisition. Their team identified gaps: assignment chain issues on P-002, open-source compliance questions on CR-001, and unresolved trade-secret incident documentation.<br><br>Every remediation decision directly affects the acquisition price. IP quality translates to enterprise value through the EBITDA multiple.`,
                    r5_s1_text: `Full IP documentation remediation program`,
                    r5_s1_hint: `Cost 200K+. Documents the trade-secret incident and the open-source audit. Cannot close an NPE case still in court.`,
                    r5_s2_text: `Selective remediation of critical gaps only`,
                    r5_s2_hint: `Cost 80K. Fixes P-002 chain and compliance audit. Leaves minor gaps for negotiation.`,
                    r5_s3_text: `Negotiate broader reps and warranties instead of fixing`,
                    r5_s3_hint: `Minimal cost. Shifts risk to post-closing. Acquirer may demand price reduction or escrow.`,
                    r5_s4_text: `Accept acquirer IP discount without remediation`,
                    r5_s4_hint: `No cost but acquirer applies 10-15% IP risk discount to enterprise value.`,
